<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('/partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>

<%- include('/partials/header') %>

<!-- HERO PHOTO -->
<section class="page-hero grounds">
  <div class="copy">
    <h1>A walk through <em>the grounds</em>.</h1>
    <div class="jp-line">境内案内　—　GROUNDS</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section class="intro">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grounds-intro">
      <div class="eyebrow-wrap"><span class="eyebrow">The Grounds</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Enter through the main gate — and <em>walk upward</em>, slowly.</h2>
        <p>Myohokkein is a temple with an unusual architectural design.<br>
A gently rising ramp winds around the Koi Garden up to the third floor,
and two domes crown the rooftop.<br>
The main hall and temple office are located on the second floor.
We warmly invite you to visit and explore the temple grounds below.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="toc">
      <h4>Fifteen places, in order</h4>
      <div class="jp-sub">境内の15の見どころ</div>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#i01">Main Gate</a><span class="jpsm">山門（正門）</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i02">Main Hall (Jusen-dō)</a><span class="jpsm">本堂（鷲山堂）</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i03">Buddhist Practice Hall (Kokū-dō)</a><span class="jpsm">道場（虚空堂）</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i04">Prayer Hall</a><span class="jpsm">祈祷所</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i05">Grave Hall</a><span class="jpsm">納骨堂</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i06">Animal Memorial Garden</a><span class="jpsm">動物供養碑</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i07">Water Purification Place</a><span class="jpsm">水行場</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i08">Temple Office</a><span class="jpsm">事務所</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i09">Restaurant "Sekai"</a><span class="jpsm">御食事処 世海</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i10">Peace Memorial Pagoda</a><span class="jpsm">平和供養塔</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i11">The Two Domes</a><span class="jpsm">ドーム</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i12">Dove Relief</a><span class="jpsm">ハトのレリーフ</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i13">Peace Declaration Stone</a><span class="jpsm">平和宣言碑</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i14">Koi Garden</a><span class="jpsm">鯉庭</span></li>
        <li><a href="#i15">Parking</a><span class="jpsm">駐車場</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ITEMS -->
<section class="item" id="i01">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-b" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/01.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">01 · Main Gate</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">01 / 15</span>
      <h3>Main Gate</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">山門（正門）— Sanmon</span>
      <p>The main gate at street level. The inscription <em>Shōchū-zan</em> is a transcription of calligraphy by the 17th-century master Hon'ami Kōetsu, copied from the tablet at the head temple Hokkekyō-ji in Chiba.</p>
      <dl class="mini">
        <dt>Hours</dt><dd>Open 7:00 — 17:00, daily</dd>
        <dt>Design</dt><dd>After Hon'ami Kōetsu (1558–1637)</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i02">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-b" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/02.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">02 · Main Hall</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">02 / 15</span>
      <h3>The Main Hall<br><em>Jusen-dō</em></h3>
      <span class="jp-name">本堂（鷲山堂）— Hondō / Jusen-dō</span>
      <p>The outer hall seats about 120 on chairs and can also serve as a concert hall. The inner sanctuary is raised one step and opens upward through the second and third floors into a domed ceiling.</p>
      <p>The great altar is stunning: a ten-by-seven-metre black-and-gold Daimandara covers the rear wall, modelled on the mandala granted by Nichiren Shōnin at the moment of his death.</p>
      <p>
        Before it rises an eight-metre Treasure Pagoda. Inside sit the Buddha and Tahō Nyorai (Many Treasures Buddha),
while four bodhisattvas emerge upward from its sides through a movable structure.
      </p>
      <p>
        The composition represents the scene of the Buddha preaching the Lotus Sūtra,
and expresses the cosmological world of the scripture itself. Above, on a lotus pedestal, stands a 400-year-old statue of Nichiren Shōnin.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i03">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-d" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/03.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">03 · Buddhist Practice Hall</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">03 / 15</span>
      <h3>Buddhist Practice Hall<br><em>Kokū-dō</em></h3>
      <span class="jp-name">道場（虚空堂）— Kokū-dō</span>
      <p>On the third floor, above the outer hall, a hall for Buddhist-practice and study — set at exactly the height of the buddhas and bodhisattvas on the Treasure Pagoda below, so that one can face them eye-to-eye. This placement mirrors the Lotus Sūtra's <em>Ceremony in the Air</em>.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i04">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-b" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/04.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">04 · Prayer Hall</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">04 / 15</span>
      <h3>Prayer Hall</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">祈祷所 — Kitō-syo</span>
      <p>Situated directly below the main hall,
the prayer hall is a quiet and solemn space where various deities are enshrined.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i05">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-c" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/05.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">05 · Grave Hall</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">05 / 15</span>
      <h3>Grave Hall</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">納骨堂 — Nōkotu-dō</span>
      <p>In Japan, it is customary for the deceased to be cremated and their ashes enshrined for ongoing ancestral remembrance and prayer.<br>
In recent years, many families have begun choosing modern indoor memorial spaces like these instead of traditional stone graves,
as they are easier to maintain and care for in urban life.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i06">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-c" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/06.JPG'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">06 · Animal Memorial Garden</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">06 / 15</span>
      <h3>Animal Memorial Garden</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">動物供養碑 — Doubutu kuyouhi</span>
      <p>Animal memorial and ossuary services are available.
At Myohokkein, pets are memorialised in a shared ossuary beneath a monument engraved with a phoenix.
The ashes of pets that have already been cremated are interred together there.</p>
      <a href="<%= rootPath %>memorial/" class="arrow">READ MORE →</a>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i07">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-a" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/07.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">07 · Suigyō-ba</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">07 / 15</span>
      <h3>Water Purification Place</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">水行場 — Suigyō-ba</span>
      <p>A small chamber for the traditional practice of <em>suigyō</em> — pouring buckets of cold water over oneself while chanting the Buddhist prayers. Performed every morning, including through the coldest months of winter.</p>
      <p>A water-deity is enshrined at the centre of the tank; three practitioners can carry out the rite at once.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i08">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-b" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/08.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">08 · Office</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">08 / 15</span>
      <h3>Temple Office</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">事務所 — Jimusho</span>
      <p>Located on the second floor along the ramp,
this is the temple office and administrative centre.<br>
Although English support is limited,
staff may sometimes be able to assist in simple English. All visitors are warmly welcome.</p>
      <dl class="mini"><dt>Hours</dt><dd>09:00 — 17:00</dd></dl>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i09">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-d" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/09.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">09 · Restaurant "Sekai"</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">09 / 15</span>
      <h3>Restaurant "Sekai"</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">御食事処 "世海" — Osyokujidokoro "Sekai"</span>
      <p>Meals are prepared by a priest with a background in professional cooking,
and are served after memorial gatherings in a traditional Japanese-style room.<br>
Fully reservation-based, each menu can be arranged according to guests’ requests.</p>
      <ul class="food-thumbs">
        <li><img src="<%= rootPath %>img/restaurant/01.jpg" width="1477" height="1107" alt="A whole fish served as sashimi on a blue platter" loading="lazy"></li>
        <li><img src="<%= rootPath %>img/restaurant/02.jpg" width="1108" height="1477" alt="Seasonal appetisers with squid, prawn and lotus root" loading="lazy"></li>
        <li><img src="<%= rootPath %>img/restaurant/03.jpg" width="1108" height="1477" alt="Beef in a green pea soup" loading="lazy"></li>
      </ul>
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/osyokujidokorosekai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="arrow">Instagram @osyokujidokorosekai ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i10">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-a" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/10.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">10 · Peace Pagoda</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">10 / 15</span>
      <h3>Peace Memorial Pagoda</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">平和供養塔 — Heiwa Kuyō-tō</span>
      <p>At the centre stands a memorial pagoda dedicated to the victims of war throughout the world.<br>
Flanking it are four smaller pagodas commemorating the victims of the Kobe air raids,
the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki, air raids across Japan,
and the Asia–Pacific War. Memorial prayers for the dead are offered here every morning.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>


<section class="item" id="i11">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-d" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/11.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">11 · Two Domes</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">11 / 15</span>
      <h3>The Two <em>Domes</em></h3>
      <span class="jp-name">ドーム — Dōmu</span>
      <p>The temple carries two domes. The roof of the main hall is a beautiful half-sphere modelled on the oldest form of Buddhist stupa — the symbol of the temple as a Buddhist sanctuary.</p>
      <p>On the roof of the five-storey wing stands a second dome — a silver skeletal frame modelled on the Hiroshima Peace Memorial Dome.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i12">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-a" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/12.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">12 · Dove Relief</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">12 / 15</span>
      <h3>Dove Relief</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">ハトのレリーフ — Hato no Relīfu</span>
      <p>A sculpted relief runs across two exterior walls between the fourth and fifth floors: six panels showing a missile (war, armament) gradually transforming into a dove (peace). With the skeletal dome above, this is the temple's visible vow for peace.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i13">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-b" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/13.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">13 · Peace Stone</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">13 / 15</span>
      <h3>Peace Declaration Stone</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">平和宣言碑 — Heiwa Sengen-hi</span>
      <p>On 13 April 1986, at the general assembly held during the founding anniversary, the congregation adopted the <em>Myohokkein Anti-Nuclear Peace Declaration</em>. Four years later, in December 1990, a stone carved with the full text was installed in the planting bed beside the main gate.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="item" id="i14">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/14.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">14 · Koi Garden</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">14 / 15</span>
      <h3>Koi Garden</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">鯉庭 — Koi Garden</span>
      <p>A small pond set within the inner courtyard, with carp circling among the stones — a quiet place to pause before continuing upward through the temple.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>



<section class="item" id="i15">
  <div class="wrap"><div class="row">
    <div class="media"><div class="ph pl-c" style="background-image:url('<%= rootPath %>img/grounds/15.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center;"></div><span class="label">15 · Parking</span></div>
    <div class="text">
      <span class="num">15 / 15</span>
      <h3>Parking</h3>
      <span class="jp-name">駐車場 — Chūshajō</span>
      <p>Visitor Parking Available</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-grid">
      <a class="cta-card image grounds-gallery" href="<%= rootPath %>gallery/">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">See more</span>
          <h3>Gallery of the grounds.</h3>
          <p>Photographs of every season, ceremony, and corner of the temple.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="arrow">Open gallery</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cta-card" href="<%= rootPath %>#access">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Plan a visit</span>
          <h3>Open daily, 9:00 — 17:00.</h3>
          <p>Myohokkein sits 1 minute walk from Shinkaichi station.
            A 20 minutes by train from Shin-Kobe station.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="arrow">Access & hours</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('/partials/footer') %>

<script src="<%= rootPath %>site.js?v=<%= assetVersion %>"></script>
</body>
</html>
